{"content":[{"c":["ANDRONICUS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Deputy of Seleucid king Antiochus Epiphanes. This Andronicus aroused the Jews by murdering Onias, the high priest, and was himself then executed by Antiochus (",{"href":"?bref=2Macc.4.31-38","r":"2Macc.4.31-38","rawR":"2Macc.4.31-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Macc.4.31-38","value":"2Macc.4.31-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Macc 4:31-38"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Officer in charge of Gerizim after Antiochus Epiphanes sacked Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Macc.5.21-23","r":"2Macc.5.21-23","rawR":"2Macc.5.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Macc.5.21-23","value":"2Macc.5.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Macc 5:21-23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Christian greeted by the apostle Paul in his Letter to the Romans (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.16.7","r":"Rom.16.7","rawR":"Rom.16.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.16.7","value":"Rom.16.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:7"},") but not mentioned elsewhere. Paul called Andronicus his kinsman. The word could mean fellow countryman, fellow Jew, member of Paul’s own family, or other relative. Andronicus may also have been a fellow prisoner for the cause of Christ, perhaps even in the same prison with Paul (",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.6.4-5","r":"2Cor.6.4-5","rawR":"2Cor.6.4-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.6.4-5","value":"2Cor.6.4-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 6:4-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.11.23","r":"2Cor.11.23","rawR":"2Cor.11.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.11.23","value":"2Cor.11.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:23"},"). Paul described him as a man of note among the apostles and recognized him respectfully as an “older” Christian."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Andronicus","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Macc 4:31-38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Macc.4.31-38","rawQueryValue":"2Macc.4.31-38","sourceRefExact":"2Macc.4.31-38"},{"anchorText":"2 Macc 5:21-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Macc.5.21-23","rawQueryValue":"2Macc.5.21-23","sourceRefExact":"2Macc.5.21-23"},{"anchorText":"16:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.16.7","rawQueryValue":"Rom.16.7","sourceRefExact":"Rom.16.7"},{"anchorText":"2 Cor 6:4-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.6.4-5","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.6.4-5","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.6.4-5"},{"anchorText":"11:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.11.23","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.11.23","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.11.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f08a9726a8302dda9ecc868fc129410a515caf924d93ed0dbd6a155b5746e292","sourceItemName":"Andronicus","sourceItemOrder":345,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Andronicus","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Andronicus","title":"Andronicus","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}